bined with H-flux, gauge bundles and perturbative higher-derivative corrections, generate a nonzero cosmological constant in a four-dimensional maximally symmetric heterotic compactification?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0019"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:0e1bff7d169dd719d9c6c02411553da2c8feb75740648acf1a7feb5803411d7e","title":"What constraints apply to the mass and coupling of a gauge boson of total lepton number over mZ′ ≈ 0–10^12 eV, and how do its neutrino couplings and absence of quark couplings change the relevant searches?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0021"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:0ef0bdcb0b0fad8ba06989de6999e721580b9184b89b5cc06b35c8591bebffee","title":"Which apparently consistent effective theories can admit a UV completion with dynamical gravity? The lectures formulate this as distinguishing the string landscape from the Swampland.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0026"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:0e737425a32644086b18219525253fe1adf9a178cea35c1e0686e07fbdd51a52","title":"What one-loop two-derivative effective action follows from bosonic-string massless amplitudes, and can its extrapolation beyond the critical dimension admit de Sitter solutions at weak coupling and small curvature?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0033"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:0e5fa87a37e1a760605dd9bbf9c019c3778c50c57a8f328b61eb130c0a3d0298","title":"The local model isolates how quickly classical acceleration restores inflaton motion after an uphill turnaround. It freezes the positive potential energy and force while keeping both scalar acceleration and Hubble friction.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0033"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:0e4f5c989b93ff5ce31